      "CultureId": "",
      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBusiness-operation validation methods must evaluate their rules through a validation collector.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat the Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Rules \u0026 Validations Collector\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; Validation rules are gathered and evaluated through a collector rather than scattered control flow. The collector runs every applicable rule and presents the resulting validation failures through one consistent mechanism. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/2.%20Services/2.1%20Foundations/2.1%20Foundations.md#213112-rules--validations-collector\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA collector evaluates all applicable rules before raising the validation result, giving callers a complete and stable account of invalid input. Ad-hoc checks fail piecemeal, duplicate exception construction, and make the service\u0027s validation policy harder to extend consistently.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STX0012: Business-operation validation methods must evaluate their rules through a validation collector.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eprivate\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estatic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Evoid\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidateStudentOnAdd\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E newStudent)\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eif\u003C/span\u003E (newStudent \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eis\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Enull\u003C/span\u003E)\n    {\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Ethrow\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Enew\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ENullStudentException\u003C/span\u003E();\n    }\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STX0012\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eprivate\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estatic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Evoid\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidateStudentOnAdd\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E newStudent) =\u0026gt;\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidate\u003C/span\u003E(\n        message: \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-string\u0022\u003E\u0026quot;Student is invalid.\u0026quot;\u003C/span\u003E,\n        (\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERule\u003C/span\u003E: \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIsInvalid\u003C/span\u003E(newStudent.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EId\u003C/span\u003E), \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EParameter\u003C/span\u003E: nameof(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EId\u003C/span\u003E)),\n        (\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERule\u003C/span\u003E: \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EIsInvalid\u003C/span\u003E(newStudent.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EName\u003C/span\u003E), \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EParameter\u003C/span\u003E: nameof(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EName\u003C/span\u003E)));\n\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eprivate\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estatic\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Evoid\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValidate\u003C/span\u003E(\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estring\u003C/span\u003E message,\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eparams\u003C/span\u003E (dynamic \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ERule\u003C/span\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estring\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EParameter\u003C/span\u003E)[] validations)\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Evar\u003C/span\u003E invalidStudentException = \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Enew\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EInvalidStudentException\u003C/span\u003E(message);\n\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eforeach\u003C/span\u003E ((dynamic rule, \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Estring\u003C/span\u003E parameter) \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Ein\u003C/span\u003E validations)\n    {\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eif\u003C/span\u003E (rule.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ECondition\u003C/span\u003E)\n        {\n            invalidStudentException.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EUpsertDataList\u003C/span\u003E(\n                key: parameter,\n                value: rule.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EMessage\u003C/span\u003E);\n        }\n    }\n\n    invalidStudentException.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EThrowIfContainsErrors\u003C/span\u003E();\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
